<article class="env-lemma" id="0A82">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A82">Lemma <span data-tag="0A82">47.18.1</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m, \kappa )$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $\omega _ A^\bullet $ be a normalized dualizing complex. Let $Z = V(\mathfrak m) \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$. Then $E = R^0\Gamma _ Z(\omega _ A^\bullet )$ is an injective hull of $\kappa $ and $R\Gamma _ Z(\omega _ A^\bullet ) = E[0]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0955" data-tag="0955">47.10.1</a> we have $R\Gamma _{\mathfrak m} = R\Gamma _ Z$. Thus 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  R\Gamma _ Z(\omega _ A^\bullet ) = R\Gamma _{\mathfrak m}(\omega _ A^\bullet ) = \text{hocolim}\  R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(A/\mathfrak m^ n, \omega _ A^\bullet )  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Lemma <a href="/tag/0954" data-tag="0954">47.8.2</a>. Let $E'$ be an injective hull of the residue field. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0A7Q" data-tag="0A7Q">47.16.4</a> we can find isomorphisms 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(A/\mathfrak m^ n, \omega _ A^\bullet ) \cong \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(A/\mathfrak m^ n, E')[0]  \]
</div>
    <p>
       compatible with transition maps. Since $E' = \bigcup E'[\mathfrak m^ n] = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(A/\mathfrak m^ n, E')$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/08Z4" data-tag="08Z4">47.7.3</a> we conclude that $E \cong E'$ and that all other cohomology groups of the complex $R\Gamma _ Z(\omega _ A^\bullet )$ are zero. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>